            <div xml:id="d162-a6-a1">

                <pb facs="0266" n="206" xml:id="pg206"/>


                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Wolff to Charles F. Burkhardt, burgomaster of Basle City.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consulate,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Basle,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 11, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Pursuant to the conversation relative to
                    the imprisonment of Charles Berry, I have herewith the honor to present you,
                    viz:</p>
                <p>1. Certificate of naturalization of Charles Berry as an American citizen.</p>
                <p>2. Renunciation of his citizenship as a Swiss.</p>
                <p>In case you should desire other papers, I can send for them to the American
                    legation at Berne.</p>
                <p>As Berry has committed no crime, I hope you will be induced to release him from
                    prison.</p>
                <p>With great respect,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. L. WOLFF.</signed></closer>



